From 154762f0a362338971fa60ce2fd5a9dfbea5de46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 03:46:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix disturbance-detection cadence bug

monitor.samples is capped at 180 entries (push+shift), so once a
monitoring session ran long enough to fill it, samples.length stayed
pinned at 180 forever. Since 180 % 60 === 0, the process() step (state
classification, sound switching, event logging, training uploads) then
fired on every animation frame (~60x/sec) instead of once per second,
causing rapid disturbance flip-flopping and event/API spam.

Fixed by tracking cadence with a dedicated, monotonically increasing
monitor.frameCount instead of the length-capped samples array.
